diff --git a/docs/profile-image-storage.md b/docs/profile-image-storage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7efd571
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/profile-image-storage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Profile image storage rollout
+
+User and organization profile images are dual-read, single-write: the
+`profile_image_file` attachment wins if present; otherwise the existing
+`profile_image` column is resolved by the original CarrierWave uploader. Uploading
+or replacing an image does not remove the legacy file or overwrite its identifier.
+No backfill or rewrite of cached image URLs is required. Other mounts (including
+tag profile images and organization cover images) still use CarrierWave.
+
+1. Keep the CarrierWave bucket or uploads volume and its URL configuration intact.
+   In S3 deployments Active Storage uses the existing bucket, region and credentials
+   (including the Forem Cloud IAM profile), writing private keys under
+   `active-storage/`. For disk storage, mount a **persistent volume shared by all
+   web and worker processes** at `ACTIVE_STORAGE_ROOT` (default `storage/`, outside
+   `public/`). Persist and back it up separately from the old uploads volume.
+2. Run `bin/rails db:migrate` before serving requests with the new code. It only
+   adds the standard Active Storage tables; old processes can keep reading the
+   same CarrierWave files. Upgrade workers and switch web traffic together so
+   requests for newly generated signed image URLs reach the new Rails proxy route.
+3. Smoke-test an unchanged profile, a replacement and a new profile. Verify the
+   published URLs return image bytes without signing in, including after a restart.
+
+Do not drop the columns, remove old files, or roll back the tables after writes
+start. A pre-Active Storage binary cannot serve attachment-only images; keep the
+reader and proxy route in any rollback release. Backfill and retirement of the
+legacy store are separate deploys.
diff --git a/lib/active_storage/service/forem_s3_service.rb b/lib/active_storage/service/forem_s3_service.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bc9af19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/active_storage/service/forem_s3_service.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+require "active_storage/service"
+require "fog/aws"
+
+module ActiveStorage
+  class Service
+    # Private S3 objects, using the same fog-aws client and credential sources as
+    # existing Forem installations. Images are served via the signed Rails proxy.
+    class ForemS3Service < Service
+      def initialize(bucket:, **credentials)
+        super()
+        @bucket = bucket
+        @client = Fog::AWS::Storage.new(credentials.compact)
+      end
+
+      def upload(key, io, checksum: nil, content_type: nil, **)
+        headers = { "Content-MD5" => checksum, "Content-Type" => content_type }.compact
+        @client.put_object(@bucket, object_key(key), io, headers)
+      end
+
+      def download(key)
+        if block_given?
+          @client.get_object(@bucket, object_key(key)) { |chunk, *| yield chunk }
+        else
+          @client.get_object(@bucket, object_key(key)).body
+        end
+      rescue Excon::Error::NotFound
+        raise ActiveStorage::FileNotFoundError
+      end
+
+      def download_chunk(key, range)
+        @client.get_object(@bucket, object_key(key), "Range" => "bytes=#{range.begin}-#{range.max}").body
+      rescue Excon::Error::NotFound
+        raise ActiveStorage::FileNotFoundError
+      end
+
+      def exist?(key)
+        @client.head_object(@bucket, object_key(key))
+        true
+      rescue Excon::Error::NotFound
+        false
+      end
+
+      def delete(key)
+        @client.delete_object(@bucket, object_key(key))
+      end
+
+      def delete_prefixed(prefix)
+        directory = @client.directories.new(key: @bucket)
+        directory.files.all(prefix: object_key(prefix)).each(&:destroy) # rubocop:disable Rails/FindEach -- Fog collection
+      end
+
+      private
+
+      def object_key(key)
+        "active-storage/#{key}"
+      end
+    end
+  end
+end
